===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/t͡ʃæt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-chat.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 chat.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|æt|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Abbreviation of {{m|en|chatter}}. The bird sense refers to the sound of its call.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}
[[image:Wikimania 2009 - Chatting (3).jpg|thumb|Two people '''chatting'''. (1) (2)]]

# To be [[engage]]d in informal [[conversation]].
#: {{ux|en|She '''chatted''' with her friend in the cafe.}}
#: {{ux|en|I like to '''chat''' over a coffee with a friend.}}
# To talk more than a few words.
#: {{ux|en|I met my old friend in the street, so we '''chatted''' for a while.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To talk of; to discuss.
#: {{ux|en|They '''chatted''' politics for a while.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Lenny Smith|title=Choices|page=43| passage=We would get totally stoned and usually drunk too and '''chat''' a load of nonsense into the small hours.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|slang|often as {{m|en|chatting}}}} To [[chat shit]] {{gloss|to speak nonsense, to lie}}.
#: {{uxi|en|Don't listen to me, I'm '''chatting'''.}}
# To exchange [[text]] or [[voice]] [[message]]s in [[real time]] through a [[computer]] [[network]], as if having a [[face-to-face]] conversation.
#: {{ux|en|Do you want to '''chat''' online later?}}
## {{lb|en|by extension|Philippines}} To send a text message via [[w:Facebook Messenger|Facebook Messenger]] instead of via [[SMS]].

