{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} [[informal|Informal]] [[conversation]].
#: {{ux|en|It'd be cool to meet up again soon and have a quick '''chat'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=Foreword|passage=Reg liked a '''chat''' about old times and we used to go and have a chinwag in the pub.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} An exchange of [[text]] or voice messages in real time through a computer network, resembling a face-to-face conversation.
#: {{coi|en|[[Internet Relay Chat|Internet Relay '''Chat''']]}}
# {{lb|en|internet|uncountable|with or without "the"}} A [[chat room]], especially (in later use) one accompanying a [[videoconference]] or [[live stream]].
#: {{ux|en|"Type yes in (the) '''chat''' if you can hear me."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1997|author=Meg Booker|title=The Insider's Guide to America Online|page=256
|passage=While there are '''chats''' for various interest groups (games, Internet, sports), you can also {{...}}}}
## {{lb|en|metonym|video gaming}} The entirety of users, viewed collectively, in a chat room, especially the chat room accompanying a [[live stream]].
##: {{ux|en|'''The chat''' just made a joke about my poor skillz.}}
##: {{ux|en|"'''Chat''', should I pick up this sword before heading out?"}}
## {{lb|en|by extension|nonstandard|humorous}} {{n-g|Familiar term of address for users on [[social media]] other than a chat room, as in "[[guys]]."}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any of various small [[Old World]] [[passerine]] [[bird]]s in the [[muscicapid]] [[tribe]] {{taxlink|Saxicolini|tribe}} or subfamily {{taxfmt|Saxicolinae|subfamily}} that feed on [[insect]]s.
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any of several small Australian [[honeyeater]]s in the [[genus]] {{taxfmt|Epthianura|genus}}.

